# Markdown abbreviations (English full name on first use)

When writing or editing any Markdown note in this repo:

1. **On the first appearance of a technical abbreviation in that file**, add the English full name in parentheses immediately after it.
2. Use **English only** in the parentheses — do **not** add Chinese glosses.
3. Format: `ABBREV (English Full Name)` or `**ABBREV** (English Full Name)`. Prefer half-width ASCII parentheses `()`.
4. Do **not** repeat the expansion on later occurrences in the same file.
5. Skip expansion if that abbreviation is **already** followed by `(...)` with an English expansion in the same file (including earlier edits).
6. Do not expand inside fenced code blocks (```), inline code with heavy signal noise, or pure filenames/paths where the token is not used as a concept (judgment call: prefer expanding when the term is taught).
7. Prefer expanding the **longest** match first (e.g. `DTLB` before `TLB`, `ACLINT` before `CLINT` if both appear).

## Examples

```markdown
# good
从 LSU (Load/Store Unit) 发起访存；后面再写 LSU 即可。
PMP (Physical Memory Protection) 查权限；PMA (Physical Memory Attributes) 查属性。

# bad — Chinese inside parentheses
LSU（Load/Store Unit，加载存储单元）

# bad — expand every time
… LSU (Load/Store Unit) … 再次 LSU (Load/Store Unit) …
```

## Common expansions (non-exhaustive)

| Abbrev | English full name |
|--------|-------------------|
| LSU | Load/Store Unit |
| TLB / DTLB / ITLB | Translation Lookaside Buffer / Data TLB / Instruction TLB |
| MMU | Memory Management Unit |
| PMP | Physical Memory Protection |
| PMA | Physical Memory Attributes |
| ASID | Address Space Identifier |
| VMID | Virtual Machine Identifier |
| VA / PA | Virtual Address / Physical Address |
| VPN / PPN | Virtual Page Number / Physical Page Number |
| PTE | Page Table Entry |
| CSR | Control and Status Register |
| AXI / AHB | Advanced eXtensible Interface / Advanced High-performance Bus |
| SRAM | Static Random-Access Memory |
| SMP / AMP | Symmetric Multi-Processing / Asymmetric Multi-Processing |
| DMA | Direct Memory Access |
| IRQ / IPI | Interrupt Request / Inter-Processor Interrupt |
| PLIC / ACLINT / MSIP | Platform-Level Interrupt Controller / Advanced Core Local Interruptor / Machine Software Interrupt-Pending |
| AMO | Atomic Memory Operation |
| CMO | Cache Management Operation |
| TCM / ITCM / DTCM | Tightly-Coupled Memory / Instruction TCM / Data TCM |
| RTOS | Real-Time Operating System |
| hart | hardware thread |
| FSM | Finite State Machine |
| AGU | Address Generation Unit |
| TRM | Technical Reference Manual |
| lr/sc | Load-Reserved / Store-Conditional |
| GPA / HPA | Guest Physical Address / Host Physical Address |
| PBMT | Page-Based Memory Types |
| NC | Non-Cacheable |

When introducing a new abbreviation not listed above, still expand it once with the conventional English full name from the relevant ISA/spec/docs.

## Context-sensitive abbreviations

Do **not** blindly expand homographs. Example:

| Context | `SPI` means |
|---------|-------------|
| GIC / interrupt controller | Shared Peripheral Interrupt |
| Board peripherals / BSP | Serial Peripheral Interface |

Pick the expansion that matches the surrounding topic.
